<report>
<line><title>McNemar and exact (Liddell) test for a paired fourfold table</title></line>
<line></line>
<line><b>Input table:</b></line>
<table>
<tr><td><in>tab_a1</in></td><td><in>tab_b1</in></td></tr>
<tr><td><in>tab_a2</in></td><td><in>tab_b2</in></td></tr>
</table>
<line></line>
<line>Uncorrected Chi<sub>2</sub> = <in>chi</in> (1 DF)  <pval><in>chi_p</in></pval></line>
<line>Yates' continuity corrected Chi<sub>2</sub> = <in>yates_chi</in> (1 DF)  <pval><in>yates_chi_p</in></pval></line>
<line></line>
<line><b>After Liddell (1983):</b></line>
<line>Point estimate of relative risk (R') = <in>risk</in></line>
<line></line>
<line><ci>Exact <in>pc</in>% confidence interval = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in></ci></line>
<line></line>
<line>F = <in>f</in></line>
<line><pval>Two sided <in>tail_2</in></pval></line>
<block name="r_prime">
<line></line>
<line><warn>R' is significantly different from unity</warn></line>
</block>
</report>
